# shadow_lower bootstrap — edit source, then promote

## Source of truth

- **Fixes always land in `cc/shadow/*.ccs` / `*.cch` first.** That is the only source of truth for parse/emit/UFCS behavior.
- Committed `cc/bootstrap/shadow_lower/MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-N/` is **regenerate-only**. Never hand-edit `include/*.h`, `shadow_lower.c`, or patch `last-good`'s tree in place to "land" a fix.
- `out/include/cc/shadow/*.h` is a **build product**, not a second source tree. Never edit those headers to fix a bug — default `make -C cc` recopies `last-good` over them and the bug returns. Never `cp` raw `*.cch` onto those paths.

## Ship loop (required when face changes should stick)

```bash
# 1. Edit cc/shadow/*.cch
# 2. Iterate (ccs rebuild) or ship (snapshot + promote + bootstrap build)
./scripts/iterate_shadow_lower.sh                 # day-to-day
./scripts/iterate_shadow_lower.sh --ship --smoke  # freeze into last-good
# 3. Human-gated commit of last-good + MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-N
```

Default `make -C cc` builds from `last-good` (`SHADOW_LOWER_SOURCE=bootstrap`). That does **not** pick up uncommitted `.cch` edits until you ccs-rebuild and promote.

## Faces vs bootstrap

- Snapshot copies lowered faces into `latest/`; promote freezes them into a new `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH-N`.
- Do not lower a single face `.cch` as a standalone TU (include fragments; can hang). Change the `.cch`, rebuild the whole lowerer, then snapshot.

